# Architecture

Keep ingestion, interpretation, inventory, ledger, imports, forecasting, and reminders as modules in one application.

- Do not add a multi-agent framework, vector database, or generic plugin marketplace.
- Models propose changes. Application code validates and calculates. Deserialize model JSON into records and validate schema, tenant, and domain rules before use. Model output never becomes a posted JPA entity directly, and a model cannot write a posted record or run arbitrary SQL.
- The owner approves. A database transaction commits local effects. External actions run as later jobs. Unknown external outcomes are reconciled, not blindly retried.
- Posted records are immutable. Corrections are linked reversals, adjustments, or credit records.

```java
// Bad: persist the model payload as the posted sale
saleRepository.save(objectMapper.convertValue(modelJson, Sale.class));

// Good: validate a draft, then post through the transactional service
SaleDraft draft = draftValidator.validate(proposal, businessId);
postingService.approveAndPost(draft, approval);
```
